    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9811" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντι-βλέπω</span></b> , fut.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-βλέψομαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					25.98
				</span></i>
			:—<i>look straight at, look in the face,</i> c.
			dat. pers., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῷ ἐμῷ πατρὶ οὐδ᾽ ἀντιβλέπειν
					δύναμαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>HG</u>
					5.4.27
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖς φίλοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Com.Adesp.</u>
					22.41
				</span></i>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς τὸν ἥλιον,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Mem.</u>
				4.7.7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>Sens.</u>
				18
			</span></i>: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς δωρεὰς βασιλέων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Comp.Dem.Cic.</u>
					3
				</span></i>
			: c. acc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιβλέπειν ἐκεῖνον οὐ δυνήσομαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Men.
					586
				</span></i>
			: abs., part., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιβλέπουσαι . . αἱ αἶγες</span>”
				<i>facing one another,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>HA</u>
					611a5
				</span></i>
			.</div>
